<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> My SCP is a cap that can telepathically talk to their victims and convinces them into believing that it's a higher being, and if they do what it demands, they'll be awarded what they truly wanted in life. When the victim completes their task(s), the SCP disappears and leaves them, so they can suffer for what they have done. (So basically, it's a troll)</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> In 2010, a man was found dead in his house from suicide. One of his friends went to check on him and saw that the door was unlocked. He decided to enter the house and noticed there were multiple drawings all over the walls and hundreds of pictures in one of the rooms of the SCP. There was also a message on one of the walls that say this,</p>
<p>&quot;I Don't Understand. I Did Everything It Wanted Me To Do, But I Don't Hear It Anymore. I Made It My God. I Pushed Everyone Away From My Life. I Killed My Own Two Kids For It, And Yet It's Abandons Me. I Guess My Fate Wasn't Good Enough&#8230;&quot;</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The cap can teleport to different places in the world, causing more harm to others. The cap does these things to people because it finds it entertaining.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I don't think I represented my central narrative the right way, but the story is going to be around addendums, interviews, and incidents.</p>
<p>The hook seems kinda dull, so I might change it tomorrow.</p>
<p>This might be a boring and cringy SCP idea, so go easy on me lol. (But seriously though, any critique is helpful.)</p>

